eola is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm flattened tan pink unremarkable nipple  Surrounding the areola along the lateral aspect is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm semicircular healed linear scar  which comes to 0 8cm of the closest superior skin margin  Also noted is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm healed linear scar along the lateral skin  which comes to 0 5cm of the lateral skin margin  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  and the posterior black  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm exposed cavity along the mid posterior aspect  On sectioning  the cavity communicates with an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 4cm cavity  which is one half blood clot and one half cavity  This area comes to 0 3cm of the anterior margin and extends up to the scar on the skin surface adjacent to the areola  No residual tumor is grossly appreciated surrounding the cavity  Also noted in the upper outer quadrant is a poorly delineated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm region of chalky yellow discoloration  consistent with fat necrosis  The remainder of the specimen displays diffuse dense nodular gray white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  Sectioning of the upper outer quadrant reveals no apparent lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity  anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Region of fat necrosis in upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved mammary tissue  medial to cavity  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Lymph Nodes  Left Axilla   Dissection PART B  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , Inferolateral_IMF_(inframammary_fold).
