ing 13 lymph nodes from the modified radical mastectomy   Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   3  including 2 lymph nodes from the modified radical mastectomy   Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   18  including 11 lymph nodes from the modified radical mastectomy   Extracapsular extension  Marked  Other forms of axillary involvement  Lymphatic vessels  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA AND LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS  3  CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR RADIATION  4  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SKIN  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF CARCINOMA  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 3 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm left simple mastectomy specimen which is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm tan nipple areolar complex with a centrally located 1 0cm in diameter grossly unremarkable nipple  The specimen is inked as follows  posterior   black  anterior   blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm irregular  stellate gray white  slightly firm area which is consistent with the prior healing biopsy site and which is located within the lower outer quadrant of the specimen  1 0cm from the posterior margin and 2 0cm from the anterior margin of the specimen  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of lobulated tan yellow fat with a moderate amount of interspersed dense gray white fibrous tissue  No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified and no lymph nodes are appreciated within the axillary aspect of the specimen  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows   REMOV