Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  AMY S  COLWELL  M D  Resident  Matija Snuderl  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Judith A Ferry  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Gregor Krings  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 49 year old woman with a history of invasive lobular carcinoma undergoing mastectomy with SLN biopsy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE WITH NO TUMOR IDENTIFIED  0 1   SEE NOTE  B  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY 1  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  2  EXTENSIVE LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  4  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE TABLE 1 AND NOTE  C  SKIN  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION SKIN AND SUBCUTIS WITH NO SIGNIFICANT PATHOLOGIC ABNORMALITY  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS   1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  4 x 4 x 2 5cm  gross measurement   GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Present  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  PERINEURAL INVASION  Present  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Positive at the posterior margin of the specimen along a broad front  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Note  Due to an issue with fixation and tissue processing  the histologic findings and immunohistochemical staining results in this case are sub optimal  Sections of the sentinel lymph node  part A  are negative for tumor and the results of immunostains for cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin on three tissue levels support the diagnosis  Sections of the main breast excision  part B  reveal diffuse invasive lobular carcinoma arising in a background of extensive lobular carcinoma in situ  Both the invasive and in situ lobular carcinoma are present at the posterior margin of the specimen  There is extensive artifact with stromal retraction present which limits assessment for the presence of lymphatic vessel invasion  however  a few foci with definitive lymphatic vessel invasion as well as peri neural invasion are identified  Immunohistochemical stains for e cadherin were performed on  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The e cadherin stain is negative in areas of invasive and in situ lobular carcinoma and supports the diagnosis  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left axilla sentinel node count    REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm lymph node which is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1 and now entirely submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a 13 x 13 x 2cm left simple mastectomy specimen oriented with a stitch designating 12 o clock  The specimen was weighed at the surgeon s request in the Frozen Section Lab and the total was 163 g  The overlying is a 3 x 2cm skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm nipple which is grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  Upon sectioning there is an ill defined cavity surrounded by fibrosis and measuring 1 x 1 x 0 5cm in the left upper outer quadrant which is grossly 0 1cm from the posterior resection margin and 0 3cm from the anterior resection margin  Adjacent to the biopsy cavity  there is a 3 x 3 x 2cm ill defined fibrotic mass with numerous firmer nodules which abut posterior resection margin and are 0 5cm from the anterior resection margin  The rest of breast tissue is firm and fibrotic  The specimen is sectioned and submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The biopsy cavity entirely submitted including closest margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Suspicious fibrotic firm area medially from the biopsy cavity with anterior and posterior resection margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional section of the firm suspicious area close to the center on the nipple   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cross section of the nipple   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Unremarkable breast parenchyma away from the lesion  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Mattison  REMOVE_MRN    left breast skin   is a 9 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm skin ellipse  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   NEGATIVE FOR METASTASIS  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 01   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 19 07PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows    The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained    Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained    Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained    The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows    Do not show overexpr